# PMAT-547 — every CI job runs on the fleet

### 1. the measurement that started it

  $ gh api repos/paiml/forjar/actions/jobs/103531462399 --jq '"\(.name)\trunner=\(.runner_name)\tlabels=\(.labels|join(","))\t\(.conclusion)"'
  dogfood-surface	runner=GitHub Actions 1000366553	labels=ubuntu-latest	success
  classify	runner=GitHub Actions 1000366551	labels=ubuntu-latest	success
  doctests	runner=GitHub Actions 1000366556	labels=ubuntu-latest	success

  The runner is read back from the API, not from the workflow file. A workflow
  that SAYS ubuntu-latest is a claim; runner_name is what actually ran it.
  `GitHub Actions <n>` is a GitHub-hosted runner.

  For contrast, the jobs that were already on the fleet, same run:

  $ gh api repos/paiml/forjar/actions/jobs/103531462466 --jq ...
  ci / lint	runner=intel-clean-room-12	labels=self-hosted,clean-room	success
  ci / coverage	runner=intel-clean-room-3	labels=self-hosted,clean-room	success
  ci / test	runner=intel-clean-room-8	labels=self-hosted,clean-room	success

### 2. the scope, before

  $ grep -rn "runs-on:" .github/workflows/ | awk -F'runs-on:' '{print $2}' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
       29  ubuntu-latest
       10  [self-hosted, clean-room]
        2  ${{ matrix.runner }}
        1  ubuntu-22.04
        1  ${{ matrix.os }}

  Plus hosted values inside three matrices: lint.yml (ubuntu-latest,
